<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see light rain and snow, cool.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see light rain and snow, cool.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies Wednesday were forecast to see light rain and snow flurries and cool temperatures, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's no significant amounts of precipitation on the Prairies today, some showers and flurries across Alberta and Saskatchewan,&quot; meteorologist Phil Wright said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see a mix of sun and cloud and highs of 0 to 7.0 Celsius. About 80 percent of crops were harvested by Monday, Alberta Agriculture said.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see scattered snow flurries in the north and east with highs of 0 to 3.0 Celsius.</p>
<p>About 89 percent of crops were harvested by Monday, Saskatchewan Agriculture said.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see scattered snow flurries with highs of -2.0 to 5.0 Celsius.</p>
<p>--Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548</p>
</text>
